hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16848","Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me from Munir ibn Abd Allah from his father from Sa'd ibn Abi Dhubab, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and accepted Islam. I said: O Messenger of Allah, grant to my people what they accept Islam upon of their wealth. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did so, and he appointed me over them. Then Abu Bakr, may Allah the Exalted be pleased with him, appointed me, then Umar after him appointed me."
